    "descriptionEn": "## Key Points\n\n- **Burden of Proof**: The one making a claim must provide evidence to support it\n- **Oath of Denial**: The defendant need only take an oath denying the claim if no evidence exists\n- **Legal Justice**: This prevents false claims from succeeding and protects rights\n\n## Lessons Learned\n\n> \"Evidence rests with the claimant; without proof, the denial under oath suffices.\"\n\n1. Claims require proof; mere accusations are insufficient\n2. This principle prevents chaos and protects innocent people\n3. Islamic justice balances protection of rights with prevention of false claims\n\n## Practical Application\n\n- *Don't make claims against others without clear evidence to support them*\n- *When accused falsely, know your right to defend yourself with an oath*\n- *Support fair justice systems that require proof before punishment*\n- *Avoid spreading accusations or rumors without verified evidence*\n- *Respect this principle in personal, business, and community disputes*",
